    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0177" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.30 Asiatic Fleet/527: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Commander in Chief, United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>)<anchor n="24" xml:id="d205-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-20">20 August, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0020. Your 0020–1040 approved except for the acceptance of offer of
                    transportation fuel and provisions from Japanese which is not approved at this
                    time. State Department recommends that in your reply to Admiral Oikawa the words
                    “recognize special situation” be deleted and instead the words “in view of
                    navigational difficulties” be substituted.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
